@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] update-screen-is-required
When the server offers a newer build, Pulls shows only the update screen from the first
frame of a start: "Pulls 0.28.0 is ready", "Update to keep using Pulls.", every version
it brings with its summary and bullets, and "Update to 0.28.0" as the main action.
Nothing closes it but the update, and Back leaves the app (rule 104).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] update-shows-its-progress
Update downloads and installs in the app and shows how far it got in place (a ring while
it downloads, the orb while the system installs). A failed download or install offers Try
again and never lets the reader through (rules 63 and 104).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] whats-new-reads-like-a-changelog
What's new shows each version as its own block: the version as a small header, a New tag
on the newest, the summary as a bold headline, one bullet per line with an accent dot, a
hairline between versions, and `### New` / `### Fixed` groups where the section has them
("Think of how good professional changelogs look", rule 127; J6).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] whats-new-opens-once
After an install the update screen did not show, What's new opens by itself once; it is
also a page of Settings and a command (rule 104).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] changelog-shows-pictures
Every changelog section from 0.40.0 on carries at least one picture of what changed, a
small GIF where it moves, and the update screen, What's new and Settings' version page
show each one under the bullet it follows, full width with the cards' corner. A version
already installed loads its pictures from the APK; a version only offered loads them from
the server beside the APK. Tavi asked for this on 16 Oct at 10:49 ("images in the
changelog too, showing the stuff, or little gifs if its animated").
